Package: Tumor2Line
Type: Package
Title: Matching Tumor-Derived Query Samples to Cancer Cell Lines with Population-Aware Transcriptomic Modeling
Version: 0.1.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Hua", "Zou", email = "zouhua1@outlook.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Bin", "Duan", email = "binduan@sjtu.edu.cn", role = c("aut"))
  )
Date: 2026-10-10
Description: Selecting cancer cell line models that faithfully represent patient
  tumors or other tumor-derived query samples is an important step toward
  improving the biological relevance and translational value of preclinical
  cancer studies. Tumor2Line provides a transcriptome-based framework for
  matching query populations, including tumors, patient-derived organoids,
  patient-derived xenografts, and related models, to candidate cancer cell lines.
  The workflow integrates expression preprocessing, a shared scaled principal
  component representation, and population-aware matching with unbalanced
  optimal transport. Known query-cell-line pairs are not required for matching
  and, when available, can be used to evaluate recovery with Top1 accuracy,
  Top3 accuracy, mean reciprocal rank, and true-pair rank. Visualization
  utilities support interpretation of candidate rankings and known-pair recovery.
